{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3049","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3049","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3049\",\"parent_revision\":\"7346952e41350200ddd3578db8ddb9a01992a0a5d96307528caac60c0cc72077\",\"root_revision\":\"7346952e41350200ddd3578db8ddb9a01992a0a5d96307528caac60c0cc72077\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a maintainer of the Codex plugin compatibility port (PR #2787), I want workflow-level (not isolated-unit) test coverage for the Codex-facing scripts, plus the 11 deferred Important-tier code findings fixed, so that a regression in the manifest-sync, MCP-discovery, or skill-activation pipelines is caught by CI before it silently corrupts repo-wide plugin manifests or skill-activation matrices.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFull finding details and rationale: `/tmp/handoff-codex-pr2787-deferred-work-2026-08-20.md` (this session's starting point). PR #2787, branch `codex-plugin-usability-port`, HEAD `40f8b70e` at time of filing. Verified current: 3 of 7 scripts already have some test coverage (`generate_codex_skill_activation_matrix.py`, `validate_codex_plugin_isolated.py`, `validate_codex_skill_activation.py` in `tests/`); the other 4 have none.\\n\\nFiled via `gh issue create` rather than `/dh:work-backlog-item create` because that skill's gate-token bang-exec line fails deterministically in this checkout (same pre-existing bug tracked as #2992, confirmed recurring here).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria Test Coverage Primary User Explicitly Rejected Isolated Unit Only Coverage\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `scripts/sync_codex_plugin_manifests.py` has a workflow-level test: run the script against a real/realistic plugin directory copy, assert resulting `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` and `.mcp.json` are valid and correctly derived \u2014 not just unit tests of helper functions.\\n- [ ] `scripts/verify_cross_harness_mcp_structure.py` + `scripts/discover_cross_harness_mcp_candidates.py` have a pipeline test proving they compose correctly end-to-end (discover \u2192 verify), plus direct tests of `inspect_tree`, `mcp_config_paths`, `plugin_root`, `rank_candidates`, `build_metadata_query`, and the `search_code()` pagination state machine.\\n- [ ] `scripts/script_utils.py` gets a dedicated test file covering `run_gh_json()`'s 4 error branches (gh not on PATH, timeout, non-zero exit, invalid JSON).\\n- [ ] `scripts/validate_codex_skill_activation.py`'s `observe_event()` gets all 5 rejection branches tested, including the `BLOCKED_ITEM_TYPES` safety-gate check (currently untested \u2014 the core safety property of the read-only activation lane).\\n- [ ] `scripts/generate_codex_skill_activation_matrix.py` gets the 4 `ValueError`/`TypeError` branches (missing name, incomplete frontmatter, unknown override, duplicate targets) and the `--check` CLI path tested.\\n- [ ] `scripts/validate_codex_plugin_isolated.py`'s `copy_auth_from_current_home()` (credential handling) and the symlink-escape guard in `create_temp_workspace()` get tests, matching the sibling script's existing pattern.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria Important Tier Code Findings\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Manifest drift: `sync_codex_plugin_manifests.py` gets a `--check` mode (mirroring `generate_codex_skill_activation_matrix.py --check`) and CI wiring so committed `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` staleness (21 of 22 manifests currently stale) is caught, not silent.\\n- [ ] `pyproject.toml`'s blanket `D`/`DOC`/`TRY` suppression for `scripts/validate_codex_skill_activation.py` is fixed: `D103`/`TRY300` must never be suppressed per `.claude/rules/linting-exceptions.md` \u2014 either narrow the suppressed codes with a real per-category justification, or fix the underlying lint issues.\\n- [ ] `sync_codex_plugin_manifests.py` expands (or explicitly errors on) unexpanded `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` placeholders in copied `mcpServers` \u2014 Codex doesn't expand them (see `docs/codex-mcp-runtime.md`).\\n- [ ] `sync_codex_plugin_manifests.py` preserves hand-curated `interface` fields (`displayName`, `category`, `defaultPrompt`) instead of overwriting them wholesale every run.\\n- [ ] GitPython `Repo` objects in `dh_paths.py` / `validate_codex_plugin_isolated.py` are used as context managers.\\n- [ ] Hang-handling (`timeout=10` + actionable \\\"unreachable network filesystem\\\" message) is restored in `dh_paths.py`'s subprocess\u2192GitPython migration.\\n- [ ] `AppServerClient._read_stdout` (daemon thread in `validate_codex_skill_activation.py`) gets exception handling so a transient read error isn't misreported as a generic timeout.\\n- [ ] `auto_sync_manifests.py`'s `.claude-plugin`/`.codex-plugin` manifest pair gets a version-agreement assertion.\\n- [ ] `generate_codex_skill_activation_matrix.py` gets a shebang, mode 755, and switches its regex frontmatter parsing to `ruamel.yaml`/`frontmatter_utils` per `.claude/rules/yaml-toml-libraries.md`.\\n- [ ] The 12,827-line committed `.checkpoint.json` at `research/claude-code-plugins/2026-08-03-cross-harness-mcp-candidate-rankings.checkpoint.json` is removed or gitignored.\\n- [ ] `validate_codex_plugin_isolated.py`'s `main()` except-tuple covers `json.JSONDecodeError` for its unguarded `json.loads()` calls (the `git` path was already fixed in commit 40f8b70e).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c8719135aad0886fd441bacf116be6e2a4888a7a1e94b29925c33a058faf400b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPuh_RA\"}"}